From e02d3e28d1915f2778797400b44bfca64c038e45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:36:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] test(host-contracts): Level 0 retirement tests for the
 ACL v0.4.1 backport

Foundry tests next to Zama's ACL tests (test/acl), v0.13 line:

- ACLRetirement.t.sol: views per role (user, delegator, delegate, contract;
  the delegated view; the gated getter; persistAllowed), inbound grants
  accepted and inert, typed errors and their precedence, ERC-165, storage
  location, retirement while paused and while deny-listed, carry during a
  pause, multicall atomicity in both orders, one-way state, revocation
  (pause-gated on this line, unchanged), and a differential fuzz against
  ACL v0.4.0 for never-retired accounts.
- ACLRetirementExemption.t.sol: a retired EIP-7702 EOA and a retired
  contract compute through the real FHEVMExecutor v0.5.0, then every export
  path reverts (allow, allowForDecryption, allowTransient, multicall,
  delegateForUserDecryption, FHE.fromExternal(h, ""), OpenZeppelin ERC-7984
  0.5.3 handle transfers and requestDiscloseEncryptedAmount), each with a
  never-retired control; the three executor invariants, pinned.
- ACLRetirementUpgradeMatrix.t.sol: U1 and the in-line guard, hazard,
  collision and lying-implementation cases (cross-line steps run on main).
- ACLRetirementGas.t.sol: gas measurements against the v0.4.0 baseline.

test/acl/retirement holds test-only fixtures (verbatim ACL sources, imports
re-pointed) and the solc 0.8.24 port of OpenZeppelin ERC-7984 0.5.3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
